{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>A woman when she emits seed.</b> 'When she emits seed' first — then 'she gives birth to a male'; 'and if a female' — she gives birth, meaning: if the man emits seed first, then she gives birth to a female, and this is the meaning of 'and if.' From here the Sages, blessed be their memory, said: a woman who emits seed first gives birth to a male; a man who emits seed first gives birth to a female. Some explain that they found in the Book of Nature that there are in a woman seven orifices: three on the right and three on the left and one in the middle. If the seed enters those on the right, she gives birth to a male; if in those on the left, she gives birth to a female; and if in the middle, she gives birth to a tumtum or an androgynus. When she lies on her right side, the seed enters those on the right and she gives birth to a male, and the impurity hastens to depart, and therefore she is impure only seven days, and her purification is after three. And when she lies on her left, she gives birth to a female, and the impurity does not hasten to depart, and therefore she is impure two weeks. And thus it is written: ״שמאלו תחת לראשי וימינו תחבקני״ — to give birth to males."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:01.414340610Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}